    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm a middle school teacher and i'm trying to put together a social studies lesson for my 7th graders about social equity and systemic reform. i want to help them understand why certain viewpoints are seen as progressive and revolutionary, and why other viewpoints are seen as more regressive or stubborn. can you help me draft a lesson plan that covers these different angles?",
