      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This is a complex topic, so framing it through current events can be very engaging for 7th graders. Begin by defining \"social equity\" versus \"equality\" using relatable examples, such as providing everyone the same size shoe versus providing shoes that fit each individual. Then, use a case study—like affordable housing or climate action—to explore different proposed solutions, labeling them as focusing on gradual reform versus sweeping systemic change. Finally, facilitate a structured debate where students argue for different approaches to see how viewpoints lead to labels like \"progressive\" or \"regressive.\"",
